  "full_text": "100.7 KSLX. And according to an interview with Joe Walsh and another one with Eagles manager Irving Azoff, yes, the band has enjoyed the way things have been going with Deacon Fry as well as Vince Gill. So they're going to do 40, 50 dates next year. We're waiting on a Phoenix one. But they're going to be touring with some interesting cats. They're going to be doing some tour dates with this country guy. They're going to be doing some dates with Jimmy Buffett. And they're going to be doing some dates with James Taylor. Very interesting. So good things. Either works for 2018 if you're a fan of live shows, but you may have to travel for that one. All the ones we've got, Audio Express, Concert Calendar, CancelLikes.com, including Robert Craig, In-Town Junking Stick Resort, Friday nights. Coming up in about a half hour, I'm going to set you up with a little head start on your Christmas shopping or whatever holiday you're shopping for. Voodoo Man Day, whatever. $50 Canola's gift card going out shortly. Keep listening for that as I come back with a song from a band who claimed that when they were recording this, they had to overdub so many... vocal parts that the acetate tapes were pretty pretty much see-through once they were done hi pappy intern here maybe you wondered why is a grown man interning at the valley toyota dealers it's for moments like this the all-new camrys are being unloaded and they are beautiful completely redesigned from the top down i used to have to camp outside the dealership but now i just sleep inside waiting for the new models easiest three months i've ever spent and the floor is so comfy i feel taller Come in today and get 0% financing for 60 months or a great week. Sometimes you get like burned out, you know. But we can do that.",
